\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {16}{\ignorespaces Production likelihood summary in the $(\eta _{10},\Sigma _H)$ plane. (a)~Filled contours of $\Delta \chi ^2(\eta _{10},\Sigma _H)$ with white contour overlays at $\Delta \chi ^2 = 2.30, 6.18, 11.83$, together with the global best-fit point and the best point on the FLRW slice $\Sigma _H=0$. (b)~The profiled anisotropy statistic $\Delta \chi ^2_{\rm  prof}(\Sigma _H)=\min _{\eta _{10}}\Delta \chi ^2(\eta _{10},\Sigma _H)$, with standard one-degree-of-freedom thresholds shown for visual reference. In the present scan the best-fit point is consistent with the FLRW slice within plotting resolution, and the profile curve should be read as the operative production constraint. Any auxiliary points beyond $\Sigma _H=0.75$ are exploratory diagnostics rather than part of the validated production interpretation.}}{40}{figure.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:chi2_inference}{{16}{40}{Production likelihood summary in the $(\eta _{10},\SigH )$ plane. (a)~Filled contours of $\Delta \chi ^2(\eta _{10},\SigH )$ with white contour overlays at $\Delta \chi ^2 = 2.30, 6.18, 11.83$, together with the global best-fit point and the best point on the FLRW slice $\SigH =0$. (b)~The profiled anisotropy statistic $\Delta \chi ^2_{\rm prof}(\SigH )=\min _{\eta _{10}}\Delta \chi ^2(\eta _{10},\SigH )$, with standard one-degree-of-freedom thresholds shown for visual reference. In the present scan the best-fit point is consistent with the FLRW slice within plotting resolution, and the profile curve should be read as the operative production constraint. Any auxiliary points beyond $\SigH =0.75$ are exploratory diagnostics rather than part of the validated production interpretation}{figure.caption.20}{}}
